cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, cite it via this metadata."
title: "hadamard-b-formal: a Lean formalization of the bordered Goethals-Seidel characterisation and the s = 1 border system"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of part of the theorem layer of the
  Hadamard-B note: twenty-six compared theorems over fifty-eight compared
  definitions. It proves an exact if-and-only-if characterisation of when a
  Goethals-Seidel array over a finite abelian group extends to a Hadamard
  matrix through a border whose strips are constant on the cosets of a
  subgroup; the house form of that characterisation, whose hypothesis is
  exactly a two-tier periodic-autocorrelation profile, together with the
  classical Goethals-Seidel theorem over an arbitrary abelian group and the
  Wallis-Whiteman/Spence bordered construction, both at an arbitrary
  reflection shift; the two row-sum consequences D5 and D6 of Theorem C, and
  only those two - the forced-parameter clauses D1-D4 and the classification
  corollary are not formalized; Lemma T, the s = 1 profile bijection, and the
  theorem that a twist fixing the reflection shift is a diagonal conjugation;
  Theorem D's clauses (D-a) through (D-e), including the degenerate-branch
  collapse (D-a') with its entry-for-entry equality of the two assemblies and
  its converse, and both directions of the (D-e) transport, packaged as an
  exactly-when; and the seed-problem bijection clause of the index-two
  collapse corollary - only that clause, the characteristic-subgroup and
  automorphism-equivariance clauses being unformalized, as is the 768-squared
  census behind (D-e). On the compared surface this resolves the s = 1,
  index-two border system in the sense of Theorem D's own clauses, subject to
  those two exclusions. Two witness records are imported under SHA-256 pins,
  cross-checked against the source repository's canonical matrix digests, and
  checked in the kernel against the hypotheses of the characterisation,
  carrying Hadamard matrices of orders 52 and 20 through the theorem rather
  than through a matrix product; no novelty of existence is claimed at either
  order, both of which are long settled. All twenty-six public theorems are
  kernel-checked with axioms confined to propext, Classical.choice, and
  Quot.sound. AI-generated formalization with a human managing the workflow -
  produced by Claude Code (Fable 5, Anthropic) with Claude Opus subagent
  lanes, and reviewed by two AI systems with no independent human expert
  review; see DISCLOSURE.md. The authors field below records the repository
  owner and responsible publisher, not a mathematical contributor; the
  AI/human division of labour is DISCLOSURE.md. The licence below is the
  licence of the whole snapshot.
